tions.sh:266`\n\n[Testing] This leaves Servlet 5 without the default profile promised by the PR and linked issue. The adjacent `servlet-5.0:jetty12-testing:test` still enables `request-parameters.included=test-parameter` and sets the matching `metadataConfig` in `instrumentation/servlet/servlet-5.0/jetty12-testing/build.gradle.kts:21-27`, so `io.opentelemetry.servlet-5.0` has only the optional `when:` profile and no instrumentation-default profile. Split that suite into a default `test` and named request-capture variant as done here, and register both collection tasks.\n</details>\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5513312046","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5513312046}],"frozen_at":1791954962,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-14T05:16:02Z","frozen_sha":"d7e0e5d791957963dd776cafc78129dd79c7447e","head_ref":"trask-request-capture-metadata","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":38511836060},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","metadata":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nMoves optional Servlet and Tomcat request-parameter capture into named test variants so baseline metadata describes instrumentation defaults.\n\nKeeps request-capture and Tomcat trace-ID request-attribute behavioral coverage. Removes the setup-only trace-ID flag from telemetry labels.\n\nExtracted from #20552 to keep the controller work in a separate PR. Refs #20546.","title":"Correct request capture telemetry metadata labels"},"mode":"publish","pr":20564,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1791952303,"generation":3,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"87aac08c3f5c4813b9df2b7860a0a090","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":[